! Keypad remapping
! Make Shift+KP_Decimal produce colon (with NumLock on)
! Column order: normal, Shift, Mode_switch, Mode_switch+Shift

! Standard KPDL key (keycode 91): dual-purpose Delete/Decimal with KEYPAD type
! NumLock flips columns 1/2 for keypad keys, so colon goes in column 1
keycode 91 = colon KP_Decimal KP_Decimal colon

! KPPT key (keycode 129): dedicated Keypad Point on some laptops (e.g. CLEVO)
! Uses TWO_LEVEL type (not NumLock-sensitive), so colon goes in column 2 (Shift)
keycode 129 = KP_Decimal colon
